            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "1,\\;2,\\;4,\\;6,\\;7,\\;7,\\;12,\\;14,\\;25,\\;72",
              "display": false
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p73-q4-request",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The range is 71 minutes. Explain why the range is not a good measure to choose to represent the spread of this dataset.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "The 72-minute stay strongly affects the range: it is 71 minutes, compared with 24 minutes without that value. The range therefore overstates the spread of most visits.",
      "worked": "With the 72-minute stay, the range is $72-1=71$ minutes. Without it, the range is $25-1=24$ minutes. The 72-minute stay is far above the other values, so it dominates the range and gives a misleading picture of the spread of most visits.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
